{"OptimizedCursorPaginator.get_result method supports negative ORM offsets whose behavior is undefined across databases, risking incorrect paging, blank pages, or data leakage": 0.9361995458602905, "Organization audit logs endpoint passes enable_advanced_features=True to paginate(), but if DRF pagination wiring does not propagate unknown kwargs to the paginator constructor, this could raise a TypeError at runtime": 0.5471704006195068, "Gating optimization on is_superuser or has_global_access may prematurely disallow optimizations for non-admins even when appropriate, changing behavior for expected high-volume reads": 0.21107059717178345, "Typo in BasePaginator.build_queryset method: code assigns to queryset.query.order_b instead of queryset.query.order_by (missing 'y'), leaving ordering unchanged and causing incorrect results for previous-page navigation when sorting by a descending field": 0.00849944818764925, "OptimizedCursorPaginator class appears duplicated and misordered in paginator.py, breaking module import and class structure": 0.20404404401779175, "get_result method (lines ~136-216) has indentation implying it belongs to a class, but the OptimizedCursorPaginator class header is only introduced later (lines 821+), causing broken class structure and potential syntax/indentation errors": 0.14433056116104126, "Duplicate OptimizedCursorPaginator class declaration can cause NameError or shadowing, making earlier methods unreachable or invalid": 0.1319999247789383, "Cursor.__bool__ returns bool(self.has_results), but has_results defaults to None, so truthiness checks on Cursor instances may silently flip control flow even when results exist": 0.049607522785663605}